    "prod_dir: where the ntuples and their file lists are; overridden by $HSCP_PROD_DIR or --prod-dir.",
    "          An empty prod_dir means the repository, so 'input/x.txt' is the file input/x.txt of the checkout.",
    "binning:  default pT cut and histogram binning; a sample may override any key with its own 'binning'.",
    "samples:  one entry per sample name. 'list' = text file with one ROOT file per line, 'file' = a single ROOT file,",
    "          both relative to prod_dir unless absolute or a URL. 'type' is data, mc or signal; 'dataset' groups",
    "          the samples of one dataset, for --dataset; 'mass' (GeV) is informative, for signal.",
    "python/Weight.py: 'xsec' (pb) of a simulated sample, and 'sum_weights' if its ntuples were skimmed or have",
    "          generator weights (default: bin 1 of EventCutflow); 'luminosity' (pb^-1, top level) or --lumi."
